 "text": "Sheridan County Register of Deeds\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nVirtual Nebraska\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's Office\nGIS Workshop\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary Discharge\nProperty Valuation Protests\nSpecial Licenses\nCounty Court Office\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict Court Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's Office\nSecretary of State\nLocal Election Results\nExtension\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nProbation\nPublic Defender\nPublic Transportation\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's Office\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's Exam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nGeneral Links\nOther Organizations\nRegister of Deeds\nPhone\n308-327-5650\nEmail\nclerk@sheridancounty.ne.gov\nAddress\nPO Box 39\nRushville, NE 69360\nSindy L. Coburn\n|\nRegister of Deeds\n|\nThe Register of Deeds has the power to take\nacknowledgments, administer oaths, and certify the same by his or\nher signature. The Register of Deeds must keep a book in which every\ninstrument filed for record in his or her office is entered and an\nofficial seal. The Register of Deeds may appoint one or more\ndeputies for whose acts the register will be responsible. The deputy\nmay not be the County Treasurer, Sheriff, Clerk or Surveyor. If a\nRegister of Deeds is not elected pursuant to Section 32-518, the\nCounty Clerk shall act as Ex-Officio Register of Deeds.\nFill-In Form 521 from Department of Revenue\nCopyright © 2019 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
